<title>USA: Unitrode board amends increase in shares.</title>
<headline>Unitrode board amends increase in shares.</headline>
<dateline>MERRIMACK, N.H. 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unitrode Corp said Tuesday that its board of directors has amended a proposal to increase the number of authorized shares to 60 million instead of 100 million.</p>
<p>If the change is approved, the stock will be split two-for-one, the company said.</p>
<p>Currently, there are 30 million common shares authorized.</p>
<p>Unitrode designs and manufactures analog/linear integrated circuits, principally to perform power management, motion control, and interface functions.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
